# Copy to /etc/vps-backup-pull.env on the backup host, or let ops/install.sh generate it.
#
# These are the same variable names secrets/<server>.<environment>.env uses, deliberately.
# One name per thing: VPS_* is something on the VPS, *_ROOT is something on this host.
# The pull writes those two roots and the log review reads them, so a single vocabulary is
# what keeps the two sides pointing at the same directories with nothing to reconcile.
#
# systemd parses this file itself rather than passing it to a shell. There is no expansion,
# no command substitution, and no quoting to strip, so write a bare value and never wrap it
# in quotes, or the quotes become part of the path.

# Where to pull from. The administrative login, not the confined deploy account.
VPS_SSH_HOST=root@vps.example.com

# On the VPS: the encrypted archives, written by its own backup timer.
VPS_ARCHIVE_DIR=/var/backups/pangolin

# On the VPS: the rotated edge access logs. Today's live file is deliberately not among
# them, because rotation is what makes a file eligible to be copied.
VPS_TRAEFIK_LOG_ARCHIVE=/var/log/traefik/archive

# On the VPS: one-off Caddy container dumps kept from before rotation existed.
VPS_BLOG_LOG_DIR=/var/log/blog/legacy

# On this host: the archives and the plaintext hostconfig tree beside them.
BACKUP_ARCHIVE_ROOT=/path/to/backup/vps

# On this host: both log sets. Separate from BACKUP_ARCHIVE_ROOT, and mode 700, because
# these are plaintext and long-lived where the archives are encrypted and pruned, and
# because query strings are logged in full so the tree is as sensitive as the log.
LOG_ARCHIVE_ROOT=/path/to/backup/vps-logs

# Key auth only, since the VPS has password auth disabled. BatchMode makes an unusable key
# fail immediately instead of hanging a timed run on a password prompt nobody sees.
SSH_OPTS=-o ConnectTimeout=15 -o BatchMode=yes
